Let a phone's shell draw pull-to-refresh that Chromium decides.

Chrome on Android refreshes a page pulled down past its top. On Aura the
same gesture is already there -- OverscrollController turns an overscroll
the page did not consume into OVERSCROLL_SOUTH, honouring
overscroll-behavior and letting inner scrollers take the pull first, and
GestureNavSimple draws an arrow and reloads -- but it is off unless
--pull-to-refresh says otherwise, and its arrow is Chromium's own.

On OHOS, OverscrollConfig::SetOhosPullToRefresh() turns it on for
touchscreens (or off) whatever the switch says and sets a callback, which
the shell bridge does for phones only. With the callback set,
GestureNavSimple adds no affordance for a pull-to-refresh: it reports
"start" with the distance a release has to reach, "pull" with the
distance pulled, "release" with whether it reloaded -- it still reloads
itself -- and "reset" if it is destroyed mid-pull. The shell draws the
indicator. History navigation by horizontal overscroll is untouched.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

